From 99420fc52db54c2976f8c57b4ad960fcb72e0d96 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@soprasteria.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 16:58:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Borg: divide armour by the monster's to-hit when
 estimating melee damage

The partial-damage estimate of a monster's melee danger subtracted the
whole armour term (armour * 75) from 150 instead of dividing it by the
monster's to-hit (3 * (level + power)). Any armour class of 2 or more
therefore gave the 5% floor, and a higher monster level lowered the hit
chance. A sleeping troll with strong blows counted as almost harmless
when deciding whether a ranged attack would wake it.

Divide by the to-hit instead. The "unique nearby" clause is dropped from
the guard: it would divide by zero for a blow with no level or power, and
it added nothing when level + power is positive.

Tracked as diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#63.

(cherry picked from commit 5c7950a25e7fb62eec1987f0fe8a4f43f4bf3984)
---
 src/borg/borg-danger.c | 7 +++----
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-danger.c b/src/borg/borg-danger.c
index 2bdfdba9b..fbbcb26dc 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-danger.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-danger.c
@@ -517,10 +517,9 @@ static int borg_danger_physical(int i, bool full_damage)
         if (!full_damage) {
             /* figure out chance that monster will hit you. */
             /* add a 50% bonus in to account for bad luck. */
-            if (borg.near.unique || (r_ptr->level + power) > 0)
-                chance
-                    = 150
-                      - (((ac * 300) / 4) / 1 + ((r_ptr->level + power) * 3));
+            if ((r_ptr->level + power) > 0)
+                chance = 150
+                         - (((ac * 300) / 4) / ((r_ptr->level + power) * 3));
             else
                 chance = -1;
 
-- 
2.53.0


From fa18e1c633103dab918fe458f5d8ea913aed628c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 17:56:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Borg: cap the partial melee hit chance at 100%

The partial melee estimate adds a 50% allowance for bad luck to the
monster's hit chance, so once armour is divided by the monster's to-hit
the chance can exceed 100% and the partial estimate of a blow can come
out above its full damage.  Cap the chance at 100% so the partial
estimate never exceeds the full-damage figure for the same blow.

(cherry picked from commit fa5b7e15a8995c969a0f9e103b65644c83de356b)
---
 src/borg/borg-danger.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-danger.c b/src/borg/borg-danger.c
index fbbcb26dc..7d178d6dc 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-danger.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-danger.c
@@ -527,6 +527,10 @@ static int borg_danger_physical(int i, bool full_damage)
             if (chance < 5)
                 chance = 5;
 
+            /* never estimate more than the full damage of the blow. */
+            if (chance > 100)
+                chance = 100;
+
             /* Modify the damage by the chance of getting hit */
             z = (z * chance) / 100;
         }
-- 
2.53.0


